<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Autonomous robots operating in dynamic environments should identify and report anomalies. Embodying proactive mitigation improves safety and operational continuity. This paper presents a multimodal anomaly detection and mitigation system that integrates vision-language models and large language models to identify and report hazardous situations and conflicts in real-time. The proposed system enables robots to perceive, interpret, report, and if possible respond to urban and environmental anomalies through proactive detection mechanisms and automated mitigation actions. A key contribution in this paper is the integration of Hazardous and Conflict states into the robot’s decision-making framework, where each anomaly type can trigger specific mitigation strategies. User studies (n = 30) demonstrated the effectiveness of the system in anomaly detection with 91.2% prediction accuracy and relatively low latency response times using edge-ai architecture.</span></p>
  
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">I </span><span id="S1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">INTRODUCTION</span></h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">As Autonomous Mobile Robots (AMRs) are increasingly deployed in dynamic and unpredictable environments, the ability to proactively detect and respond to anomalies is critical for ensuring safety and operational continuity <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>. Traditional AMRs operate with limited situational awareness, often reacting to problems only after they occur, which can lead to safety incidents, operational disruptions, and reduced system reliability <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>. A key requirement in autonomous robotics is therefore proactive anomaly detection—robots must not only navigate safely but also anticipate and proactively respond to hazards for mitigation before they escalate into critical situations <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.
Past work has explored reactive safety systems and obstacle avoidance <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, but many approaches remain restricted to predefined scenarios, lacking adaptability to new anomalies or changing environments. The early models relied on rule-based or threshold detection methods <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, which did not capture contextual information or provide meaningful responses. More recent machine learning approaches combine visual perception and semantic reasoning to improve anomaly detection <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>, <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.06768v1/figs/explaining_abnormally.png" id="S1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/286;" width="429" height="286" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 1: </span>The AMR detects abnormalities during normal operation and proactively responds through real-time reporting and mitigation planning to ensure safety.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Recent advances in large language models (LLMs) and vision language models (VLMs) open new opportunities for intelligent anomaly detection <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>, <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>. These models process multimodal inputs, understand the context, and generate human-like reasoning about hazards and conflicts <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite>. Previous studies emphasize aligning robot behavior with human safety expectations to support trust in real-world deployments <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>, <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>, <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>]</cite>. In particular, VLMs improve AMR perception by integrating visual and textual understanding: Grad-CAM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite> highlights salient regions, VLFM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> allows semantic mapping, and BLIP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> grounds image–text pairs for hazard identification. These capabilities have been extended to explainable AI safety frameworks that link anomaly detection with autonomous decision making <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>, <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>.
To address current limitations, we propose a proactive anomaly detection and mitigation system that generates real-time hazard assessments and automated responses for AMR operations. Using VLFM and LLM, our approach integrates camera-based perception, semantic analysis, and language-based reasoning for contextual anomaly detection. A key innovation is the explicit modeling of two distinct anomaly states, Hazardous and Conflict, each linked to targeted mitigation strategies. This work extends our previous research on explainable safety systems <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>, <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite> with expanded anomaly detection capabilities and a real-time ROS2 implementation using AI models on the edge. Our results demonstrate improved safety, faster response, and more transparent decision-making, underscoring the potential of VLFMs and LLMs to enhance operational reliability of AMRs in dynamic environments.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PROBLEM FORMULATION</span></h2>

<div id="S2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Autonomous mobile robotic systems operating in dynamic environments must proactively detect and respond to anomalies to ensure safety and operational continuity. We define the proactive anomaly detection and mitigation task as a tuple of perception information from the data in the robot world.</span></p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\text{robot}}=\left(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{G},\mathcal{P},\mathcal{A},\mathcal{M},\mathcal{H},\mathcal{L},\mathcal{R},\varepsilon\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">robot</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒜</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℳ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℋ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℛ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\text{robot}}=\left(\mathcal{S},\mathcal{G},\mathcal{P},\mathcal{A},\mathcal{M},\mathcal{H},\mathcal{L},\mathcal{R},\varepsilon\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where, </span><math id="S2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}=(\mathbf{q},\mathbf{v},\mathbf{q}_{\text{env}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐯</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">env</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}=(\mathbf{q},\mathbf{v},\mathbf{q}_{\text{env}})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the state of the robot, with </span><math id="S2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as the position and orientation of the robot, </span><math id="S2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐯</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{v}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as the velocity of the robot, </span><math id="S2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{\text{env}}^{j}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">env</mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{\text{env}}^{j}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents the relative state of an observed environmental object. These objects might represent a hazardous situation from the robot’s point of view and can be defined. </span><math id="S2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}\equiv\mathbf{q}_{g}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒢</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}\equiv\mathbf{q}_{g}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the goal in the robot workspace. </span><math id="S2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}=\pi:[0,T]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒫</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}=\pi:[0,T]\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the planned trajectory that maps time to robot location and velocities, so that the robot safely transitions from the initial state </span><math id="S2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{0}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to </span><math id="S2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{q}_{g}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐪</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{q}_{g}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> while avoiding detected anomalies and maintaining operational safety. </span><math id="S2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{A}=\{a_{t}\mid t\in[0,T]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒜</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{A}=\{a_{t}\mid t\in[0,T]\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the set of anomalies detected during execution, where each </span><math id="S2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> includes the type of anomaly, severity assessment, the state of the robot, the relative state of the objects, and contextual information through multimodal analysis.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}=\{m_{t}\mid t\in[0,T]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℳ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}=\{m_{t}\mid t\in[0,T]\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the set of mitigation actions triggered in response to detected anomalies, where each </span><math id="S2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents automated responses such as path replanning, emergency stops, or alert notifications. </span><math id="S2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}\subset\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℋ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\subset\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents the subset of known hazardous states in which the robot is previously exposed to risk of loss, with </span><math id="S2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> being the set of all possible world states. </span><math id="S2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}\subset\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℒ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}\subset\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents the subset of loss states in which accidents or undesirable results occur. </span><math id="S2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}=\{R_{i}(\mathbf{S}_{h})\mid i\in[1,n]\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℛ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" fence="true" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}=\{R_{i}(\mathbf{S}_{h})\mid i\in[1,n]\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the set of risk functions that map hazardous states to loss probabilities, where each </span><math id="S2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}(\mathbf{S}_{h})\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}(\mathbf{S}_{h})\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents the probability of transitioning from a hazardous state to a specific loss class. </span><math id="S2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the anomaly detection effectiveness score that reflects the system’s ability to identify and respond to threats, measured through detection accuracy and response time metrics.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The set of safety constraints, anomaly detection requirements, and mitigation protocols can be formalized as a set of operational constraints </span><math id="S2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{safety}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{safety}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, which must be satisfied at all times.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S2.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{\text{safety}}=\bigcap_{i\in M}\Omega_{i}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">safety</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">⋂</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mrow></munder><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{\text{safety}}=\bigcap_{i\in M}\Omega_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where </span><math id="S2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents the constraints imposed by the safety requirement </span><math id="S2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> from the set of governing rules </span><math id="S2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. For this purpose, which can be modeled in different categories as suggested in </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><span id="S2.p6.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[</span><a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">23</a><span id="S2.p6.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">]</span></cite><span id="S2.p6.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">II-A</span> </span><span id="S2.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Hazard as Risk for Loss</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Any state that has a risk or probability of transitioning to a loss state is a hazardous state. In other words, an autonomous robot at any given time of </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{R}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{R}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> can be represented by the state </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> that belongs to the general world </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}\in\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}\in\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents the set of all possible states. Even though all feasible world states are not known, this formulates the problem by separating known and unknown subsets of the world. Let us also assume that there exists a subset of </span><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Hazardous</span><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> states, named </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}\subset\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℋ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒲</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}\subset\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> where the robot is in a state exposed to risk of loss. Similarly, in practice, all these states are not identified and an unknown subset of hazardous states might exist. Hence, this set is dynamic and, if any loss occurs, the states that ended up in a loss event should be added to </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, the hazardous subset.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmremark1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_remark">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmremark1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Remark 1</span></span><span id="Thmremark1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> </span>(<span id="Thmremark1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Robot World</span>)<span id="Thmremark1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmremark1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmremark1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Representing the robot’s world </span><math id="Thmremark1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{\text{robot}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">robot</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{\text{robot}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> in the universal state space </span><math id="Thmremark1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{W}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒲</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{W}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and state </span><math id="Thmremark1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmremark1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> that is dependent on the autonomy architecture, capabilities and limitations of the robot’s perception technology and the context at the scenario. However, for the purposes of formulating this problem, the world as perceived from the autonomous robot’s point of view consists of the spatio-temporal information of the robot and relative items in its surroundings.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmdefinition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hazardous State</span>)<span id="Thmdefinition1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">A state </span><math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is identified as hazardous state </span><math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> if </span><math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{S}_{h}\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{S}_{h}\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> exists, which means that there is a potential source of harm with the possibility of leading to a loss. The source might be originating from the malfunctioning of a system component or exposure to world states.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Risk of loss</span>)<span id="Thmdefinition2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The risk of loss is the likelihood that a hazardous state ends up in a loss state in a limited time. A probabilistic function </span><math id="Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}(\mathbf{S}_{h})\in[0,\&gt;1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐒</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">h</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"> 1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}(\mathbf{S}_{h})\in[0,\&gt;1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> can represent the likelihood of that specific incident. This risk assessment can also be utilized for explainability purposes, allowing the system to communicate the probability of different loss scenarios to users and operators, thus improving transparency in decision-making processes.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">METHODOLOGY</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The objective is to calculate a safe, feasible and anomaly-aware path </span><math id="S3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, while maximizing </span><math id="S3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> through novel anomaly detection and mitigation modules, to improve safety and operational reliability during robot navigation in dynamic environments. Our approach consists of four parts.</span></p>
<ul id="S3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1)</span><span id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Development of a multimodal anomaly detection system using VLM and LLM.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2)</span><span id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Deployment in an AMRs for real-time validation.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3)</span><span id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Integration with an autonomous navigation stack.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4)</span><span id="S3.I1.i4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Integration of proactive mitigation strategies for hazardous states.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption 1</span></span><span id="Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The effectiveness of the anomaly detection module is quantified by a scalar <em id="Thmassumption1.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_upright">anomaly detection factor</em> <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, which reflects how well the robot can identify and respond to environmental threats. The value of <math id="Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math> is determined through performance metrics that include detection accuracy, false positive rates, and response time measurements.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmassumption1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=\begin{cases}0,&amp;\text{if anomaly detection is inactive},\\
\hat{\varepsilon}\in(0,1],&amp;\text{if anomaly detection is active}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">if anomaly detection is inactive</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">if anomaly detection is active</mtext><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=\begin{cases}0,&amp;\text{if anomaly detection is inactive},\\
\hat{\varepsilon}\in(0,1],&amp;\text{if anomaly detection is active}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmassumption1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmassumption1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where, <math id="Thmassumption1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> is a normalized score derived from detection performance metrics and response time evaluations.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<figure id="algorithm1" class="ltx_float ltx_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="algorithm1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span>Anomaly Detection and Mitigation Module via VLM, Heatmap and LLM</figcaption>
<div id="algorithm1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_lst_numbers_left ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algorithm1.6.1" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">1</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Initialize LLM Node and Anomaly Detection Module;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.2" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">2</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Subscribe to topics </span><span id="algorithm1.6.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’camera/image’</span><span id="algorithm1.6.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><span id="algorithm1.6.2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’blip/caption’</span><span id="algorithm1.6.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><span id="algorithm1.6.2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">’heatmap/summary’</span><span id="algorithm1.6.2.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.3" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">3</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Set anomaly detection factor </span><math id="algorithm1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.4" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">4</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Set AnomalyDetectionModuleEnabled flag;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.5" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">while</span><span id="algorithm1.6.5.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><em id="algorithm1.6.5.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">robot is navigating</em><span id="algorithm1.6.5.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">do</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.6" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.6.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.6.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">5</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.6.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Receive image from camera stream;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.7" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.7.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.7.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">6</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.7.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Detect potential anomalies using VLM Node;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.8" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.8.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.8.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">7</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.8.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Generate visual saliency map using Heatmap Node;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.9" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.9.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.9.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">if</span><span id="algorithm1.6.9.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><em id="algorithm1.6.9.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">anomaly is detected</em><span id="algorithm1.6.9.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.9.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.10" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.10.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.10.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.10.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.10.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">if</span><span id="algorithm1.6.10.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><em id="algorithm1.6.10.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">AnomalyDetectionModuleEnabled</em><span id="algorithm1.6.10.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.10.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">then</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.11" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.11.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.11.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.11.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.11.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.11.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">8</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.11.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Classify anomaly as Hazardous or Conflict using LLM Node;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.12" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.12.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.12.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.12.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.12.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.12.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">9</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.12.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Trigger appropriate mitigation action based on classification;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.13" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.13.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.13.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.13.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.13.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.13.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">10</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.13.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Generate natural language description of detected anomaly;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.14" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.14.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.14.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.14.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.14.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.14.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">11</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.14.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Overlay and display heatmap with anomaly classification;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.15" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.15.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.15.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.15.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.15.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.15.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">12</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.15.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Save image, heatmap, and anomaly report with timestamp;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.16" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.16.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.16.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.16.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.16.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.16.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">13</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.16.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Update anomaly detection factor </span><math id="algorithm1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\leftarrow\varepsilon+\Delta\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\leftarrow\varepsilon+\Delta\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.16.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.17" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.17.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.17.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.17.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> end if</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.18" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.18.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.18.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.18.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">14</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.18.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Update navigation path to avoid detected anomaly;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.19" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.19.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.19.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> end if</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.20" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.20.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:1px;height:100%;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span><span id="algorithm1.6.20.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">15</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.20.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Execute current navigation step;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.21" class="ltx_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.21.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">end while</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.22" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.22.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">16</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.22.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Analyze anomaly detection performance metrics (e.g., detection accuracy, response time);</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.23" class="ltx_listingline">
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="algorithm1.6.23.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">17</span></span>
          <span id="algorithm1.6.23.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Correlate performance with anomaly detection factor </span><math id="algorithm1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algorithm1.6.23.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">;</span>
</div>
<div id="algorithm1.6.24" class="ltx_listingline">
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Anomaly Detection Model</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The robot is equipped with a modular anomaly detection model implemented as four ROS2 nodes, 1) Camera node, 2) BLIP node, 3) Heatmap node and 4) LLM node which will be explained in the experimental section. Each node is responsible for a distinct function. These nodes communicate through ROS topics, enabling scalable and seamless integration with existing navigation systems. This node presents information in a structured format for the classification and mitigation of anomalies, enhancing safety in dynamic environments. The camera captures a single image on request, the LLM node must be initialized first, followed by the Heatmap and BLIP nodes.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span>1 </span>Anomaly Detection Model Formulation</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To formally define our anomaly detection model, let </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represent the raw image input captured by the robot camera. The anomaly detection function </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> maps the visual input, the heatmap analysis, and the language model output to a structured anomaly classification by:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A:(X,H,L)\rightarrow\mathcal{C}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A:(X,H,L)\rightarrow\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n\times 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times n\times 3}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the image captured at resolution </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m\times n</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H=g(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H=g(X)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the heatmap function that highlights the salient regions, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L=f(X,H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L=f(X,H)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents the captioning output of the language model and </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the final anomaly classification produced. The heatmap generation function </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(X)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is given by Grad-CAM activation </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{c}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p3.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{i,j}=ReLU\left(\sum_{k}\alpha_{k}A_{c}^{i,j}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{i,j}=ReLU\left(\sum_{k}\alpha_{k}A_{c}^{i,j}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the weight for the feature map </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A_{c}^{i,j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A_{c}^{i,j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents the activation at the spatial location </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ReLU(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ReLU(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> ensures positive activation contributions. The final anomaly classification </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p5.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is derived using</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=LLM(\psi(H,X))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒞</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=LLM(\psi(H,X))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi(H,X)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">X</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi(H,X)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the feature representation that combines the heatmap and the image context and </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LLM(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LLM(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a large language model (e.g. Generative Pre-trained Transformer 3.5 Turbo) trained for anomaly classification obtained in the LLM Anomaly Detection Prompt box. The anomaly classification generated by the LLM, which depends on the environmental context and perception input and the variables related to the robot interface, captured as uncertainty </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒰</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{U}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p7.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, which reflects the confidence of detection, the accuracy of the classification and the reliability of the response.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p8" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=f\left(\mathcal{C},\mathcal{U}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒞</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒰</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=f\left(\mathcal{C},\mathcal{U}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Performance metrics will allow us to determine </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS1.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> more precisely.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.6" class="ltx_text">III-A</span>2 </span>Latency Optimization for Real-Time Anomaly Detection</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Latency is critical in real-time safety systems. The total anomaly detection time </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">total</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is defined as:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{total}}=T_{\text{camera}}+T_{\text{BLIP}}+T_{\text{heatmap}}+T_{\text{LLM}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">total</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">camera</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">BLIP</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">heatmap</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">LLM</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{total}}=T_{\text{camera}}+T_{\text{BLIP}}+T_{\text{heatmap}}+T_{\text{LLM}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{camera}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">camera</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{camera}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the image acquisition time, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{BLIP}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">BLIP</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{BLIP}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the processing time in the vision language, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{heatmap}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">heatmap</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{heatmap}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the heatmap generation time, and </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{LLM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">LLM</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{LLM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the time required for the large language model to generate an anomaly classification. Since LLM processing is performed remotely, LLM request latency </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{LLM}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">LLM</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{LLM}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p3.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> can be modeled as</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{LLM}}=T_{\text{network}}+T_{\text{processing}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">LLM</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">network</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">processing</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{LLM}}=T_{\text{network}}+T_{\text{processing}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{network}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">network</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{network}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents the latency of network transmission and </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{processing}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">processing</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{processing}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the cloud-based inference time. To minimize </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{total}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">total</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{total}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p5.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, one can formulate the optimization problem as</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{\lambda}\sum_{i}T_{i},\quad\text{s.t.}\quad T_{\text{total}}\leq T_{\text{max}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">min</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">total</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mtext></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{\lambda}\sum_{i}T_{i},\quad\text{s.t.}\quad T_{\text{total}}\leq T_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where, </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p7.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> represents hyperparameters tuning latency trade-offs and </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{max}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{max}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p7.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the maximum allowable latency for real-time safety operation.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Empirical analysis showed that latency is inversely correlated with compute power </span><math id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p8.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T_{\text{total}}\propto\frac{1}{C}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">total</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∝</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T_{\text{total}}\propto\frac{1}{C}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.SSS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">where increasing computing power reduces processing time.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.06768v1/figs/flowchart_abnormally.png" id="S3.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/241;" width="429" height="241" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 2: </span>Workflow of anomaly detection and explanation and emergency call.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">EXPERIMENTS</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To validate the effectiveness of our anomaly detection and mitigation module, we conducted structured experiments using a mobile robot running ROS 1 Noetic on a Raspberry Pi 4B with a built-in camera. The robot ROS 1 autonomy stack can communicate with the ROS 2 abnormally module. However, we tested manual and autonomous navigation scenarios with various types of anomaly to evaluate detection accuracy and response effectiveness.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.6" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Experimental Setup</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The experiments were carried out in an academic indoor environment that included a makerspace lab and a hallway (2.5m × 14m) to simulate real-world deployment conditions with controlled anomaly scenarios. The anomaly detection module, originally built in ROS 2 Humble, was adapted to ROS 2 Foxy and deployed separately for compatibility with the MYAGV robot. The images were captured every 5 seconds and processed through the Camera, BLIP, Heatmap, and LLM nodes, with real-time anomaly classifications delivered via heatmap overlays and automated mitigation actions.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" color="#000000" height="212.21" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 477.38 212.21" width="477.38"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,212.21) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 0 L 0 206.3 C 0 209.56 2.64 212.21 5.91 212.21 L 471.47 212.21 C 474.73 212.21 477.38 209.56 477.38 206.3 L 477.38 0 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 1.97 L 1.97 188.1 L 475.41 188.1 L 475.41 1.97 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 196.69)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">LLM Anomaly Detection Prompt</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 166.68)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:31.37em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:11.05em;font-size:10pt;" height="162.51" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="434.07"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:31.37em;">
<span id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">”You are a mobile robot that monitors your environment for potential hazards and conflicts. The image caption is: ’</span>{<span id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">caption</span>}<span id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">’. The heatmap analysis shows: ’</span>{<span id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">heatmap_summary</span>}<span id="S4.SS1.p2.pic1.2.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">’. Analyze this information and classify any detected anomalies. If you detect a hazard (e.g., dangerous objects, environmental threats, safety violations), respond with ’HAZARDOUS: [brief description]’ and ’REPORT’. If you detect a conflict (e.g., navigation conflicts, operational disruptions, rule violations), respond with ’CONFLICT: [brief description]’ and ’AVOID’. If no anomalies are detected, respond with ’CLEAR: [brief description of normal conditions]’ and ’RESUME’.”</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.6" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Navigation and Testing Conditions</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The experiments were carried out under four scenarios:</span></p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Manual Navigation:</span><span id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> As Test 1 - With and without anomaly detection.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Autonomous Navigation:</span><span id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> As Test 2 - With and without anomaly detection.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For each test, we recorded navigation metrics and anomaly detection output, allowing us to isolate the impact of proactive anomaly detection as represented in Table </span><a href="#S4.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ IV-B Navigation and Testing Conditions ‣ IV EXPERIMENTS ‣ Embodied Hazard Mitigation using Vision-Language Models for Autonomous Mobile Robots" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a><span id="S4.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<table id="S4.T1.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T1.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T1.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_l ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Metric</span></th>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">WoAD</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T1.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">WAD</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.T1.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
